export anchor SpreadsheetStyle:
    number: 70
    screen: TodayMobile
    name: Spreadsheet
    idea: The Today list is a live worksheet with lettered columns, numbered rows, a formula bar showing the selected cell and sheet tabs for navigation.
    base: light
    palette:
        desk: #eceef1, the page around the workbook
        cell: #ffffff, every cell and the active tab
        gridline: #d3d7dd, 1px cell borders, decorative only
        header: #f1f2f4, column letters, row numbers, bars and tabs, with #4a5260 text
        text: #1c2129, cell values, with muted #555e6c for project lines
        selectionTeal: #0b6e74, the selected cell border and handle, the active tab, the add button and focus
        selectionFill: #e3f2f2, inside the selected cell, with #cfe6e6 on its column and row headers
        todayFill: #fff3c4, Due today status cells with #6e4a00 text
        overdueFill: #fde2e0, the Overdue cell with #9e1c14 text, also the High flag and badge
        doneFill: #e1f1e4, the Done cell with #1f6130 text
    type:
        System sans, system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial,
        sans-serif, at 13px with 1.35 line height for cells. The title row
        is 17px bold, task names 13px semibold, project lines 12px muted
        and section bands 11px bold caps. Times, durations, the name box
        and the formula use ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas at 12px, right
        aligned for numbers. Column letters and row numbers are 11 to 12px
        centred.
    layout:
        A phone-width workbook up to 390px with a 1px grey frame, centred
        on the desk. From the top come a title bar with a teal grid file
        icon, Brightwork and Today.sheet, and a square teal avatar. Then a
        toolbar with All, Due today and Overdue filter toggles, Sort and a
        filter icon. Then a formula bar with the name box B9, an italic fx
        and a TASK formula for the selected task. The grid has a row number
        column and columns A, B and C, with a sliver of column D on wide
        screens. Row 1 merges into the title Monday 2 November, row 2 holds
        6 tasks, 2 meetings with a COUNT formula hint, then a Meetings band,
        a header row Time, Meeting, Length and two meeting rows. A Tasks
        band follows with header row Due, Task and project, Status, and six
        task rows where the project wraps under the name in the same cell.
        Cell B9 is selected. A status bar sums the selection, and sheet tabs
        Today, Projects, Inbox and Me with a square teal add button form the
        bottom bar.
    spacing: A 4px unit. Cells pad 4px by 6px. Nothing has gaps, everything butts against gridlines.
    density: High. All eight items and every header fit on one phone screen.
    corners: Square everywhere, 2px at most on buttons, the badge and the avatar.
    borders: 1px gridlines on every cell. The selected cell has a 2px teal border and a small square fill handle at its bottom right corner, and its column letter and row number turn teal and bold.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Small square-ended line icons from 11 to 18px. Status cells use a
        conditional fill plus a word and a shape, a filled dot for Due
        today, a ring for Upcoming, a tick for Done and a triangle for
        Overdue. High priority is a small red flag with the word High.
    focus: A 2px teal outline drawn inside the cell or field, like a cell selection.
    tone: Terse and literal like column headers, such as Due, Task, Status and Length.
